---
name: styles
type: registry:style
title: Styles
description: Design tokens with three selectable theme presets (default, secondary, tertiary).
dependencies:
  - tailwindcss
  - tw-animate-css
  - shadcn-svelte
  - "@fontsource-variable/inter"
files:
  - path: registry/items/files/styles/globals.css
    type: registry:file
    target: "~/styles/globals.css"
  - path: registry/items/files/styles/theme.css
    type: registry:file
    target: "~/styles/theme.css"
  - path: registry/items/files/styles/theme-secondary.css
    type: registry:file
    target: "~/styles/theme-secondary.css"
  - path: registry/items/files/styles/theme-tertiary.css
    type: registry:file
    target: "~/styles/theme-tertiary.css"
---

A CSS-first token set for `@tailwindcss/v4`, split into a base theme (`theme.css`) plus two alternate presets (`theme-secondary.css`, `theme-tertiary.css`). `globals.css` wires up the Tailwind imports and pulls all three in — swap the active preset per-page or per-user by setting `data-theme="theme-secondary"` (or `theme-tertiary`) on `<html>`; omit the attribute for the default palette.

`globals.css` also imports `shadcn-svelte/tailwind.css`, which registers the `data-open`/`data-closed`/`data-active`/etc. custom variants and the `accordion-down`/`accordion-up` keyframes that installed components (like `accordion`, `dialog`, `dropdown-menu`, `sheet`, `tooltip`) rely on for their open/close animations. Without it those components still work, but render without transitions.

```ts
document.documentElement.dataset.theme = "theme-secondary"; // or "theme-tertiary"
```

Each preset only overrides `--primary`, `--ring`, `--sidebar-primary`, `--selection`, and the `--chart-*` scale — everything else (background, foreground, card, border, radius) is shared, so switching presets only changes the accent, not the whole surface.

Files land in `styles/` at the project root. Import `globals.css` once from your root layout:

```svelte
<script>
  import "../../styles/globals.css";
</script>
```
